# A getter, a setter and a method are written in a literal (L1) that is handed out, so nothing is proven of their `this`. By the names that they use it is an object created below the literal, made by Object.create two steps below.
# It is an expectation with its test, as `this` of a method of a class: the entry is guarded and the accesses are typed.
# RUN(GETTER): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# GETTER: b0(v0: L{{*}}?ParameterOfEscapedFunction
# GETTER: = GetSlotOrUndefined v0 {{*}}key="_body" receivers=[L{{*}}] level=Expected
# RUN(SETTER): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# SETTER: = PutSlotOrAdd v0, v1 {{*}}key="_body" receivers=[L{{*}}] level=Expected
# RUN(METHOD): walk f4 mechanisms=all
# METHOD: = GetSlotOrUndefined v0 {{*}}key="_body" receivers=[L{{*}}] level=Expected
# -- source: this-of-a-member-written-in-a-literal-is-expected-to-be-of-the-literal-or-created-below-it.js
